# This repo's source is CRLF by convention (*.py, *.spec, *.ini) and is
# deliberately LEFT UNLISTED here, so git keeps that convention and we avoid a
# churny one-time renormalization of the source files. Do NOT add a blanket
# "* text=auto" rule -- it would try to normalize those files to LF.
#
# Only the LF-native files are protected from the Windows mount's silent CRLF
# drift (zero churn: they are already LF in the index, so declaring eol=lf just
# makes git compare normalized content and stops phantom "modified" diffs).
.gitignore  text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf

# Binary assets (future-proofing)
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
